From a394212d9213933457f8456786bd7b91005870e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:36:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Batch: transient term of the heat equation by kernels

The behaviour integrator `TransientHeatTransfer` (rate of the enthalpy,
whose gradient is the temperature at the integration point) is supported
by the kernels:

- new kinds of gradients `TEMPERATURE_3D` and `TEMPERATURE_2D`, whose
  gradients are the values of the unknowns at the points, computed from the
  values of the shape functions (`areGradientsUnknownsValues`), the
  operator `B` of a node being the value of its shape function in the
  gradients, inner forces, stiffness matrices, diagonals and action
  kernels;
- the behaviours are recognised by their structure: one scalar gradient,
  one scalar thermodynamic force, the derivative of the force with respect
  to the gradient;
- `supportsKernels` compares the kind of the gradients of the behaviour to
  the computations of the behaviour integrator (values or derivatives of
  the unknowns, external state variable updated from the unknowns), instead
  of refusing the integrators whose gradients require the shape functions;
- `areUnknownsValuesExternalStateVariables` distinguishes the temperature
  of the stationary heat transfer behaviours, an external state variable,
  from the values of the unknowns needed by the gradients.

`TransientHeatTransfer` was only declared in 3D: it is now declared for
all the hypotheses whose factories are built (3D, plane strain, plane
stress), its integration points having the weights of these cartesian
hypotheses.

Tests: new behaviour HeatStorage (rate of the enthalpy with a volumetric
heat capacity depending on the temperature). HeatTransferKernelsTest adds
the transient term to two materials in 3D and to one material in plane
strain and plane stress: the transient term changes the temperature (9 to
17%), and the integration by batches, the kernels (assembled tangent and
tangent applied without assembly), with and without prediction, give the
results of the integration point by point to 2e-15. The variants on the
debug device and on two processes only use the behaviours generated by the
generic interface. Six mutations (gradient, inner forces, operator B,
values of the shape functions, operator of the second node on the GPU,
recognition of the behaviours) are detected.
